 INPUT CARD>! Provenance / changes vs. caa005bIRCCML1stdef2TZVPP.inp and ...TZVPPa.inp:     
 INPUT CARD>! - TZVPP.inp: requested $HESS HESS=READ with no Hessian data actually supplied;
 INPUT CARD>!   GAMESS silently fell back to HESS=GUESS. Optimization proceeded but the     
 INPUT CARD>!   BFGS-updated Hessian developed an increasingly negative curvature eigenvalue
 INPUT CARD>!   (-15 -> -18 -> -30 -> -57 across successive steps) and the structure collaps
 INPUT CARD>!   (multiple H...H / X...H distances under 1.0 Angstrom in the final geometry).
 INPUT CARD>! - TZVPPa.inp: same molecule, no $HESS/$GUESS override (defaulted to HUCKEL).  
 INPUT CARD>!   Did not collapse, but 84 individual SCF single-points computed during the   
 INPUT CARD>!   NSERCH=5 numerical Hessian block (tiny finite-difference displacements)     
 INPUT CARD>!   scattered across ~0.18 Hartree (~113 kcal/mol) -- clear evidence of the SCF 
 INPUT CARD>!   landing on different, inconsistent electronic solutions step to step.       
 INPUT CARD>!   Run aborted at NSERCH=5 with GRADIENT OUT OF RANGE.                         
 INPUT CARD>! - Both runs used $FORCE METHOD=SEMINUM despite GAMESS explicitly reporting    
 INPUT CARD>!   analytic gradients were available for this SCFTYP/DFTTYP/PCM combination.   
 INPUT CARD>!   Semi-numerical gradients are noisier; that noise feeds directly into the    
 INPUT CARD>!   BFGS Hessian update, plausibly explaining both the runaway negative         
 INPUT CARD>!   curvature (TZVPP) and the erratic per-step SCF/gradient behaviour (TZVPPa). 
 INPUT CARD>!                                                                               
 INPUT CARD>! This version (b):                                                             
 INPUT CARD>! - Uses METHOD=ANALYTIC (removes the confirmed noise source)                   
 INPUT CARD>! - No $HESS or $GUESS override -- clean HUCKEL default, no stale-file risk     
 INPUT CARD>! - SOSCF=.T. restored (GAMESS's own more robust default; testing showed        
 INPUT CARD>!   SOSCF was NOT the cause of the TZVPP collapse, so no reason to avoid it)    
 INPUT CARD>! - NOTE: first submission attempt of this file mistakenly set DIIS=.T.         
 INPUT CARD>!   together with SOSCF=.T. GAMESS treats these as mutually exclusive           
 INPUT CARD>!   convergers and aborted immediately (error 911) before any SCF cycle.        
 INPUT CARD>!   Fixed by removing DIIS=.T. and keeping SOSCF=.T. alone.                     
 INPUT CARD>! - NOTE (correction): $FORCE METHOD actually governs how the HESSIAN is        
 INPUT CARD>!   computed (needed for HSSEND=.T. and periodic IHREP recomputation),          
 INPUT CARD>!   NOT the routine per-step optimization gradient -- that was already          
 INPUT CARD>!   analytic by default in every prior run (NUMGRD=F). Requesting               
 INPUT CARD>!   METHOD=ANALYTIC triggers GAMESS's analytic DFT Hessian, which has           
 INPUT CARD>!   5 requirements; RHF and non-meta-GGA were already satisfied, so             
 INPUT CARD>!   NOSYM=1, DIRSCF=.TRUE., and $CPHF CPHF=AO were added to satisfy the         
 INPUT CARD>!   rest, avoiding a fallback to the numerical-Hessian noise we are             
 INPUT CARD>!   trying to eliminate in the first place.                                     
 INPUT CARD>! - Cartesian coordinates (DLC=.F. AUTO=.F.) rather than delocalized internal   
 INPUT CARD>!   coordinates, since this is a weakly-bound 3-molecule H-bonded cluster and   
 INPUT CARD>!   automatic bond perception across long/weak intermolecular contacts is a     
 INPUT CARD>!   plausible additional source of a poorly conditioned optimization -- worth   
 INPUT CARD>!   isolating as a variable given TZVPP (which collapsed) used DLC=.T. AUTO=.T. 
 INPUT CARD>!   and TZVPPa (which did not collapse) used Cartesian.                         
